    decision: No shared design-system base; Gnomon only for now, other drafts parked
    rationale: 'Founder: rejected the thin base; ''for now we can ignore all of design systems other than gnomon for paradigm'''
  - id: d2
    decision: Gnomon is desktop-only; a true mobile version comes later as its own work
    rationale: Founder direction during the narrow-header board
  - id: d3
    decision: '''Make it standing'' opens the grant card instead of approving from a toast'
    rationale: A toast is never a decision key; Aegis found the one-gesture approval plus a focus-jump hazard
  - id: d4
    decision: Toasts anchor to the chat column's right edge below the chat header; top right above the scrim while a sheet is open
    rationale: Under the pill they covered the stack head's decision keys (Mika); Luna refined the placement
errors_encountered:
  - description: Session thread ran git stash on the shared working tree to test a baseline while a builder was mid-batch; the pop failed on a hook log
    resolution: Restored by checking out the hook file, popping, and re-appending its lines; warned the builder; no edits lost. Never stash a shared tree; read HEAD with git show instead
  - description: focusCard fell back to any gate-class card when its own card was missing, so a toast key could put the user on the wrong decision
    resolution: Caught in Mika's second review; focus targets only the exact cardId with a warn naming the missing card (ui/card-focus.ts)
learnings:
  - 'Rendered review catches what tests don''t: the toast/stack overlap, the 31px Workshop column, the voice-voice label, the missing key hover'
  - 'The Atelier UI gate parses ## Rendered for absolute screenshot paths; globs fail it'
  - atelier check (dev CLI) needs absolute paths; relative paths report 'No UI files' (a-atelier bug)
  - 'Record outranks code: night titles snapped to the recorded 13.5 rather than the shipped 17'
